TCVTROWPS2PH[H,L] flushed FP16 denormal results to zero

ISE 319433-057, TCVTROWPS2PH[H,L]: "Input FP32 denormals become FP16 zeros on
outputs. This instruction can produce FP16 denormal outputs. (MXCSR.FTZ only
controls FP32 and FP64 denormal outputs)."

Both handlers converted under prepare_ne_softfloat_status_helper(true), whose
FTZ=1 makes f32_to_f16 flush every FP16 denormal result: 2^-15, 2^-16 and
2^-24 all became 0 instead of 0x0200, 0x0100 and 0x0001. The status keeps
DAZ=1 for the FP32 inputs and now has FTZ=0.

Fixed in avx/amx_avx512.cc. Found 2026-09-29 while checking the other AMX
floating-point instructions against the ISE after the AMX-FP8 fix; upstream
master has the same code.

diff --git a/cpu/avx/amx_avx512.cc b/cpu/avx/amx_avx512.cc
index 3a25828..f942fd6 100644
--- a/cpu/avx/amx_avx512.cc
+++ b/cpu/avx/amx_avx512.cc
@@ -105,7 +105,9 @@ void BX_CPP_AttrRegparmN(1) BX_CPU_C::TCVTROWPS2PHL_VphTrm(bxInstruction_c *i)
   }
 
   // "round to nearest even" rounding mode is used when doing each convertion below.
+  // FP32 denormal inputs become zero, but FP16 denormal results are kept (ISE: no FTZ here).
   softfloat_status_t status = prepare_ne_softfloat_status_helper(true);
+  status.softfloat_flush_underflow_to_zero = false;
 
   // convert the fp32 source elements to fp16 and place them in low 16-bits of each dword
   for (unsigned n=0;n < DWORD_ELEMENTS(BX_VL512); n++)
@@ -128,6 +130,7 @@ void BX_CPP_AttrRegparmN(1) BX_CPU_C::TCVTROWPS2PHH_VphTrm(bxInstruction_c *i)
 
   // "round to nearest even" rounding mode is used when doing each convertion below.
   softfloat_status_t status = prepare_ne_softfloat_status_helper(true);
+  status.softfloat_flush_underflow_to_zero = false;
 
   // convert the fp32 source elements to fp16 and place them in high 16-bits of each dword
   for (unsigned n=0;n < DWORD_ELEMENTS(BX_VL512); n++)
